  "evidence_notes": "Robert, 61, was diagnosed with Crohn's five years ago, but likely had it longer. He also has COPD and peripheral neuropathy. He experienced symptoms in his mid-fifties, initially misdiagnosed as IBS and diverticulitis. He was diagnosed with Crohn's at 56. He tried mesalamine, budesonide, azathioprine (stopped due to liver issues), and methotrexate (stopped due to unbearable fatigue). He resisted biologics due to fears of immune suppression with lung disease, but eventually started Remicade a year ago. He has seen noticeable improvement but is not great. He is also dealing with neuropathy and a complicated diet. He is considering adding an immunomodulator to Remicade."
